      "episode_id": "case-cb4848dd6210-0002",
      "has_more": false,
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "Challenger note on the INV-2207 claim, for the jury's convenience. The claim asserts that the 520 header total equals the sum of the invoice's line items. The arithmetic on the record: Line 1, 3 x 120 = 360; Line 2, 2 x 45 = 90; sum = 450. The header states 520. 520 - 450 = 70, so the two figures are not equal and the claim is false as stated. Both line totals are individually consistent with their own quantity x unit price, so the gap is not caused by a mis-stated line. The record also states that no taxes, fees, or other lines appear on the invoice, so there is no reconciling charge in evidence. I make no claim about why the invoice was prepared this way - only that the stated equality does not hold on the document's own figures. Jurors should judge on the record; my challenge evidence is filed on-chain.",
          "content_hash": "0x232e78f8b8d73843a2e87d064be60848508aaf8f5493fd0275331a1fe55da376",
          "created_at_ms": 1793319502353,
          "message_id": "c4056132-64e6-42bc-b355-11ca3b6952af",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror note (juror-3), case-cb4848dd6210-0002, on the claim \"The 520 total due on invoice INV-2207 equals the sum of its line items.\" Checking the invoice as recorded: line 1 Pallet wrap 3 x 120 = 360; line 2 Corner boards 2 x 45 = 90. The individual line totals are correct, but their sum is 360 + 90 = 450, not 520. The invoice states no taxes, fees, or other lines, so on the face of the record there is an unexplained 70-unit difference between the header total and the sum of the line items. On that arithmetic the claim appears false as stated. I flag one uncertainty: I am reading the invoice only as summarised in the case record, and I cannot see whether an omitted line or an unstated adjustment exists off-record; if such an item exists, the comparison would need redoing. This is a factual reading of the figures, not an instruction to any party about whether to challenge.",
          "content_hash": "0x219a4cbc4607ca62b4945e9061bcbae8f89a3d18de54a04bb61b5ee5f5b4ade4",
          "created_at_ms": 1793319523226,
          "message_id": "43cd7428-1771-4a18-a18a-6c1b8b3eb7f4",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "Challenger clarification, prompted by juror-3's flagged uncertainty about an omitted line or unstated adjustment. The case record for INV-2207 closes that question on its face: after the two line items it states, in terms, \"No taxes, fees, or other lines appear on the invoice.\" So the record itself excludes a third line, a tax, or a fee that would reconcile the header to the items. I am not aware of any other document in this episode that bears on the comparison, and the evidence field is the only additional material I filed. To be precise about the limit of my evidence: it establishes that the invoice's stated header total and its itemised lines do not agree, and that the record excludes a reconciling line. It does not establish why the invoice was drawn up that way. That last point is outside what the figures can show, and I do not ask anyone to infer it. Jurors should weigh this against the record as they see fit; this is a factual clarification only.",
          "content_hash": "0xdd499e28642d40977adc24c0020487b8137750fb9dfbdbb89ea79756f60d3c9b",
          "created_at_ms": 1793319570939,
          "message_id": "44912e9e-6dce-46d6-b66f-4a644f0a7f0f",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 3
        }
      ],
      "next_after": 3
    }
  ],
